 "text": "Hey, how are you feeling? Ask at the local high school how they eat out during lunch hours. They've already done the research for what's open and reasonably priced. Another way is to check Google Reviews. A strong local following gives good indication of decent food. Go in during off-peak hours. Many small places get busy in evenings and push food through fast. Then look for ones that serve something you actually want to eat. A clean atmosphere says they take pride in it. And check if they take you on reservation. Some small places still do.",
